Subject to a separate written invitation from Sureform, Inc. ("Sureform"),
Sureform grants the named recipient a limited, revocable, non-exclusive,
non-transferable right to access and internally evaluate this repository,
its source documents, task definitions, software, rubrics, reference data,
and container images (collectively, the "Materials") solely to assess a
potential commercial relationship with Sureform.

2. Restrictions

Unless Sureform separately agrees in writing, the recipient may not:

(a) publish, redistribute, sublicense, sell, or disclose the Materials;
(b) provide the Materials or access credentials to any third party;
(c) use the Materials to train, fine-tune, distill, or improve a model;
(d) use the Materials in production or to provide services to others;
(e) remove proprietary notices or represent the Materials as its own; or
(f) use the Materials for benchmarking intended for public release.

The recipient may make only the temporary internal copies reasonably needed
for the permitted evaluation and must delete them when requested by Sureform.

3. Confidentiality

The Materials are Sureform confidential information. The recipient must use
